WEBVTT

1
00:00:53.708 --> 00:00:54.792
Here we go.

2
00:00:56.004 --> 00:00:57.234
What are you doing?

3
00:00:57.235 --> 00:00:58.375
We're gonna be late.

4
00:00:58.376 --> 00:00:59.356
Seven P's, honey:

5
00:00:59.357 --> 00:01:01.748
Proper prior planning prevents
piss poor performance.

6
00:01:01.749 --> 00:01:02.990
This isn't cool, Mom.

7
00:01:02.991 --> 00:01:04.278
No, it is not cool.

8
00:01:04.279 --> 00:01:05.932
But you know what is cool?

9
00:01:05.933 --> 00:01:07.164
Your game was delayed until 7:00.

10
00:01:07.165 --> 00:01:08.566
You got three hours to kill.

11
00:01:09.657 --> 00:01:11.198
Why didn't you tell me?

12
00:01:11.199 --> 00:01:12.600
I literally just told you.

13
00:01:14.002 --> 00:01:15.266
Does dad know?

14
00:01:15.267 --> 00:01:16.637
No.

15
00:01:16.638 --> 00:01:18.969
I think he'll figure it out
when he gets to the field.

16
00:01:19.827 --> 00:01:21.238
That's messed up.

17
00:01:21.239 --> 00:01:22.373
Totally messed up.

18
00:01:27.195 --> 00:01:30.607
Great, now I have more time to worry.

19
00:01:30.608 --> 00:01:32.619
It's just a scrimmage, sweetheart.

20
00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:33.860
Yeah, but I'm supposed to be on my way

21
00:01:33.861 --> 00:01:37.674
to MVP stardom in college
like you were, so.

22
00:01:37.675 --> 00:01:40.597
Yeah, well, I don't care
so much about the MVP stardom

23
00:01:40.598 --> 00:01:42.659
as I do that free ride
so I don't have to pay

24
00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:44.371
for that college tuition.

25
00:01:44.372 --> 00:01:46.073
Speaking of, maybe you could help me

26
00:01:46.074 --> 00:01:47.700
with that financial aid application.

27
00:01:52.290 --> 00:01:54.211
Sweetie, I was just joking
about the scholarship.

28
00:01:54.212 --> 00:01:55.713
It's okay if you don't get it.

29
00:01:59.347 --> 00:02:02.619
Samantha, what is it?

30
00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:03.621
Nothing.

31
00:02:04.902 --> 00:02:05.903
Not nothing.

32
00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.985
I want you to talk about this.

33
00:02:08.986 --> 00:02:10.077
I know.

34
00:02:10.078 --> 00:02:11.418
Whenever it is, you can say it.

35
00:02:11.419 --> 00:02:12.420
I know!

36
00:02:16.074 --> 00:02:17.225
Is someone out there?

37
00:02:21.399 --> 00:02:23.044
I don't see anything.

38
00:02:26.753 --> 00:02:28.450
- Sweetheart-
- Don't touch me!

39
00:02:31.766 --> 00:02:35.296
You don't know how I
feel when I see its face.

40
00:02:37.863 --> 00:02:38.864
Whose face?

41
00:02:41.669 --> 00:02:42.670
Honey.

42
00:02:43.941 --> 00:02:45.893
Baby, I need you to keep talking to me.

43
00:02:47.135 --> 00:02:48.136
It's nothing.

44
00:02:49.997 --> 00:02:51.948
Nothing, it's...

45
00:02:51.949 --> 00:02:53.204
I can't play tonight.

46
00:02:55.333 --> 00:02:56.334
Hey.

47
00:03:06.422 --> 00:03:07.423
Fuck off!

48
00:03:26.004 --> 00:03:27.027
You got a game to play.

49
00:03:30.218 --> 00:03:31.888
Sweetie, I'm trying to
respect your privacy,

50
00:03:31.889 --> 00:03:32.990
but you're scaring me.

51
00:03:34.101 --> 00:03:35.202
I'm gonna assume you can't hear me

52
00:03:35.203 --> 00:03:36.804
'cause you've got headphones on.

53
00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.283
Okay, I'm coming in.

54
00:03:56.354 --> 00:03:57.355
Oh, my God.

55
00:07:27.615 --> 00:07:29.966
Ally, we're out of time.

56
00:07:29.967 --> 00:07:32.819
I'm really sorry, but we have to move on.

57
00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:34.130
We're turning over your patients

58
00:07:34.131 --> 00:07:35.796
to someone else in the practice.

59
00:07:36.674 --> 00:07:38.676
We really did try to work with you here.

60
00:07:42.339 --> 00:07:44.771
Hey, Ally, it's Terry.

61
00:07:44.772 --> 00:07:46.373
I know a therapist.

62
00:07:46.374 --> 00:07:48.304
I know, I know, you're
probably rolling your eyes.

63
00:07:48.305 --> 00:07:50.276
Why talk to another therapist?

64
00:07:50.277 --> 00:07:53.500
Trust me, it was a lifesaver
for my sister when dad died.

65
00:07:53.501 --> 00:07:55.081
And listen, I hope you don't mind,

66
00:07:55.082 --> 00:07:57.054
but I relayed your contact info, so-

67
00:08:24.923 --> 00:08:26.842
- It's not my time yet.

68
00:08:50.296 --> 00:08:51.965
For the love of God.

69
00:09:02.309 --> 00:09:03.954
Hi, Ally?

70
00:09:05.082 --> 00:09:06.083
I'm Jan.

71
00:09:07.635 --> 00:09:09.345
I heard that you weren't doing very well,

72
00:09:09.346 --> 00:09:12.218
so I felt that I should come by in person.

73
00:09:12.219 --> 00:09:13.490
Who are you?

74
00:09:13.491 --> 00:09:14.842
I'm a psychologist.

75
00:09:16.834 --> 00:09:18.128
Oh, okay, yeah.

76
00:09:19.597 --> 00:09:20.587
Yeah, Terry mentioned you.

77
00:09:20.588 --> 00:09:22.699
He said you were a lifesaver.

78
00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:25.482
He didn't tell me you'd be so attentive.

79
00:09:25.483 --> 00:09:27.504
Since I'm here, I
would just like to make sure

80
00:09:27.505 --> 00:09:30.547
that you're not a danger to yourself.

81
00:09:30.548 --> 00:09:31.949
And then, I'll be on my way.

82
00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:34.695
Five minutes, that's all I need.

83
00:09:35.743 --> 00:09:36.744
Sure, yeah.

84
00:09:40.017 --> 00:09:42.670
No parent should
ever have to Bury her child.

85
00:09:48.626 --> 00:09:52.218
I appreciate you coming,
it's a really lovely gesture.

86
00:09:52.219 --> 00:09:53.109
I don't need your help.

87
00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:54.430
I'll be fine.

88
00:09:54.431 --> 00:09:56.553
Humor me for a moment.

89
00:09:56.554 --> 00:09:59.319
And then I'll walk out that
door and never bother you again.

90
00:10:00.648 --> 00:10:01.649
Sure.

91
00:10:04.461 --> 00:10:06.557
Would you like to see
your daughter again?

92
00:10:08.135 --> 00:10:11.261
Samantha, would you like to see her?

93
00:10:12.429 --> 00:10:14.331
Because I'm sure she wants to see you.

94
00:10:15.212 --> 00:10:17.051
Why would you say that to me?

95
00:10:18.616 --> 00:10:21.688
You want to know why, why she did it?

96
00:10:21.689 --> 00:10:22.933
It's perfectly natural.

97
00:10:24.692 --> 00:10:26.146
She can tell you herself.

98
00:10:28.786 --> 00:10:30.156
I think it's time that you left.

99
00:10:30.157 --> 00:10:32.328
I am not going to beat around the bush.

100
00:10:32.329 --> 00:10:34.961
As a therapist yourself, you
know there is a lot of bullshit

101
00:10:34.962 --> 00:10:35.963
in this business.

102
00:10:38.636 --> 00:10:40.695
Just hear me out.

103
00:10:56.173 --> 00:10:57.197
This works.

104
00:10:58.495 --> 00:11:00.516
I know because I've done it.

105
00:11:00.517 --> 00:11:02.158
What is it?

106
00:11:02.159 --> 00:11:03.160
It's tea.

107
00:11:04.672 --> 00:11:06.623
It's been brewed with a
hallucinogenetic flower

108
00:11:06.624 --> 00:11:08.675
called Datura stramonium.

109
00:11:08.676 --> 00:11:11.007
And you want me to drink that?

110
00:11:11.008 --> 00:11:12.009
Just a little bit.

111
00:11:15.680 --> 00:11:17.764
I wouldn't see Sam,
I'd see a hallucination.

112
00:11:17.765 --> 00:11:20.566
The psychedelic effects
are inconsequential.

113
00:11:20.567 --> 00:11:22.019
It's what happens afterwards.

114
00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:24.131
And what's that?

115
00:11:25.653 --> 00:11:27.077
I was in your shoes once.

116
00:11:28.596 --> 00:11:32.980
I drank the tea and
then I saw him, my boy.

117
00:11:36.213 --> 00:11:39.199
My son who had been
murdered 20 years prior.

118
00:11:41.228 --> 00:11:43.864
You have no idea how good
it felt to hug him again.

119
00:11:47.284 --> 00:11:49.760
This is a way to know.

120
00:11:50.878 --> 00:11:54.024
To see what Samantha saw,
to feel what she felt.

121
00:11:57.014 --> 00:11:59.066
Are you ready to take that leap of faith?

122
00:12:00.317 --> 00:12:02.019
Why would I believe any of this?

123
00:12:04.611 --> 00:12:06.263
Because you're still listening.

124
00:12:13.961 --> 00:12:15.612
There's a door to the other side.

125
00:12:17.404 --> 00:12:18.478
This opens that door.

126
00:12:23.991 --> 00:12:26.493
Give me call when you're
ready to walk through it.

127
00:16:05.049 --> 00:16:06.786
Do you believe in ghosts?

128
00:16:11.558 --> 00:16:12.732
That's an odd question.

129
00:16:15.051 --> 00:16:17.107
I think it's odd that
I don't know the answer.

130
00:16:19.156 --> 00:16:21.527
It's 95 degrees outside.

131
00:16:21.528 --> 00:16:23.990
This afternoon I saw a kid in a scarf,

132
00:16:23.991 --> 00:16:25.492
bundled up in winter clothing.

133
00:16:26.974 --> 00:16:28.452
I thought that was odd.

134
00:16:30.177 --> 00:16:31.678
No, I don't believe in ghosts.

135
00:16:38.342 --> 00:16:39.345
I saw a therapist today.

136
00:16:39.346 --> 00:16:41.148
She says she thinks she can help me.

137
00:16:42.319 --> 00:16:43.320
Yeah?

138
00:16:44.801 --> 00:16:45.802
You went outside?

139
00:16:46.587 --> 00:16:48.139
Oh, no, she came here.

140
00:16:49.026 --> 00:16:50.241
Why?

141
00:16:50.242 --> 00:16:51.187
I don't know.

142
00:16:51.188 --> 00:16:53.413
She's unconventional I guess.

143
00:16:53.414 --> 00:16:54.498
I guess so.

144
00:16:56.583 --> 00:16:58.867
If she's not in our network
we can't afford her.

145
00:16:58.868 --> 00:17:00.991
Can you just humor me on this?

146
00:17:02.279 --> 00:17:04.420
It's just me working now.

147
00:17:04.421 --> 00:17:05.922
I can't keep doing this alone.

148
00:17:08.365 --> 00:17:10.046
Well, we don't have a kid to
put through college anymore,

149
00:17:10.047 --> 00:17:11.339
so there's that.

150
00:17:11.340 --> 00:17:12.891
Is that supposed to be funny?

151
00:17:14.111 --> 00:17:15.112
No.

152
00:17:17.124 --> 00:17:18.024
I don't know why I said that.

153
00:17:18.025 --> 00:17:19.026
I'm sorry.

154
00:17:20.257 --> 00:17:22.772
How many handles of vodka
are in that kitchen right now?

155
00:17:24.381 --> 00:17:25.632
Or pills in the bathroom?

156
00:17:29.446 --> 00:17:30.646
Okay, you made your point.

157
00:17:30.647 --> 00:17:31.648
Have I?

158
00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:34.001
You want therapy?

159
00:17:34.962 --> 00:17:36.599
Go outside.

160
00:17:36.600 --> 00:17:38.094
That's not fair.

161
00:17:38.095 --> 00:17:40.486
You can't keep living in this house,

162
00:17:40.487 --> 00:17:42.268
hiding with her memory forever.

163
00:17:42.269 --> 00:17:44.131
How is this so easy for you?

164
00:17:44.132 --> 00:17:45.745
She's gone!

165
00:17:47.124 --> 00:17:48.125
Okay?

166
00:17:49.356 --> 00:17:50.357
That's it.

167
00:17:56.363 --> 00:17:57.364
I'm sorry.

168
00:18:03.400 --> 00:18:05.152
It's not easy for me.

169
00:18:19.556 --> 00:18:21.308
Okay, hey, future Sam.

170
00:18:22.189 --> 00:18:25.091
This is a recording on my song.

171
00:18:25.092 --> 00:18:26.593
Let's hope I don't mess it up.

172
00:18:31.779 --> 00:18:32.844
♪ You're in space ♪

173
00:18:32.845 --> 00:18:37.291
♪ But I don't know where ♪

174
00:19:01.076 --> 00:19:02.993
Samantha?

175
00:19:32.706 --> 00:19:34.280
- Now?
- There's someone outside

176
00:19:34.281 --> 00:19:35.282
in the backyard.

177
00:19:38.986 --> 00:19:39.819
I'm calling the police.

178
00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:41.497
Well, now, hang on a second.

179
00:19:41.498 --> 00:19:42.678
Who's outside?

180
00:19:42.679 --> 00:19:44.679
Someone wearing a mask.

181
00:20:01.758 --> 00:20:02.759
I see it.

182
00:20:03.590 --> 00:20:05.392
That's what's gonna take us to hell.

183
00:20:06.482 --> 00:20:08.046
What?

184
00:20:08.047 --> 00:20:09.708
Why would you say that?

185
00:20:09.709 --> 00:20:10.870
I don't see anything.

186
00:20:12.132 --> 00:20:13.573
Why would I say what?

187
00:20:13.574 --> 00:20:16.612
- About us going to hell?
- What?

188
00:20:16.613 --> 00:20:17.614
I never said that.

189
00:20:19.226 --> 00:20:21.828
Jesus, Ally, it's like
you're on drugs or something.

190
00:20:23.859 --> 00:20:25.611
No, I'm just spooked, that's all.

191
00:20:28.055 --> 00:20:29.494
What are you doing?

192
00:20:29.495 --> 00:20:31.466
- I'm gonna call 911.
- No!

193
00:20:31.467 --> 00:20:32.668
If you call the cops
they'll be poking around

194
00:20:32.669 --> 00:20:34.470
till 5:00 A.M. taking statements.

195
00:20:34.471 --> 00:20:35.741
We both need our sleep.

196
00:20:35.742 --> 00:20:36.712
So, what, I'm supposed to just let

197
00:20:36.713 --> 00:20:38.784
a crazy person roam around my backyard?

198
00:20:38.785 --> 00:20:39.885
No, it was nothing.

199
00:20:39.886 --> 00:20:41.917
I just thought I saw Sam go downstairs.

200
00:20:41.918 --> 00:20:43.849
And then I thought I saw
her go in the backyard.

201
00:20:43.850 --> 00:20:45.255
You thought you saw Sam?

202
00:20:47.133 --> 00:20:49.114
Clearly my imagination
is playing tricks on me.

203
00:20:49.115 --> 00:20:50.116
I'm sorry.

204
00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.033
Did you see anyone
in the backyard or not?

205
00:20:55.021 --> 00:20:56.022
No.

206
00:20:59.906 --> 00:21:00.907
Where are you going?

207
00:21:02.108 --> 00:21:03.169
To take a look.

208
00:21:03.170 --> 00:21:04.490
Why, why would you do that?

209
00:21:04.491 --> 00:21:07.777
To make sure everything's okay, for you.

210
00:21:30.282 --> 00:21:31.283
Well?

211
00:21:33.560 --> 00:21:35.575
Just your imagination like you thought.

212
00:21:36.973 --> 00:21:38.594
Look, if it makes you feel any better,

213
00:21:38.595 --> 00:21:40.005
I once thought I saw
something creeping around

214
00:21:40.006 --> 00:21:41.120
in the backyard too.

215
00:21:42.999 --> 00:21:43.967
What was it?

216
00:21:43.968 --> 00:21:47.017
I don't
know, the neighbor's cat.

217
00:22:30.557 --> 00:22:31.667
Hello?

218
00:22:31.668 --> 00:22:33.038
You said that for me to know why

219
00:22:33.039 --> 00:22:34.741
I'd need to see what Samantha saw?

220
00:22:35.642 --> 00:22:37.857
It's good to hear
from you again, Ally.

221
00:22:39.596 --> 00:22:40.897
It is possible...

222
00:22:42.359 --> 00:22:43.869
Did she tell you that?

223
00:22:43.870 --> 00:22:45.891
That I needed to see these things?

224
00:22:45.892 --> 00:22:47.383
Communicating with the other side

225
00:22:47.384 --> 00:22:50.035
isn't as simple as picking up a phone.

226
00:22:50.036 --> 00:22:52.882
We need to figure out what
Samantha is trying to say.

227
00:22:54.693 --> 00:22:57.016
Is it possible I'm
already seeing what she saw?

228
00:22:58.345 --> 00:22:59.880
Are you?

229
00:22:59.881 --> 00:23:00.882
What did you see?

230
00:23:02.939 --> 00:23:03.940
I saw...

231
00:23:05.942 --> 00:23:07.744
Ally, did you drink the tea?

232
00:23:09.836 --> 00:23:10.837
I took a sip.

233
00:23:11.558 --> 00:23:13.062
What did you see?

234
00:23:16.212 --> 00:23:18.688
I saw someone in
the backyard watching me.

235
00:23:19.646 --> 00:23:21.677
And I know it's the same
thing that Samantha saw

236
00:23:21.678 --> 00:23:24.039
because she drew a picture of it.

237
00:23:24.040 --> 00:23:25.691
You took the leap.

238
00:23:25.692 --> 00:23:28.097
Samantha is already trying to communicate.

239
00:23:31.648 --> 00:23:33.122
So, what do I do now?

240
00:23:34.110 --> 00:23:35.611
Talk to me.

241
00:23:35.612 --> 00:23:37.242
We have a few chats.

242
00:23:37.243 --> 00:23:38.408
I'll help you find her.

243
00:23:45.238 --> 00:23:46.722
I don't know if we can afford that.

244
00:23:46.723 --> 00:23:49.385
You don't need
to worry about that.

245
00:23:49.386 --> 00:23:52.338
We'll try a couple of
sessions, no pressure.

246
00:23:52.339 --> 00:23:54.029
I'll come to you.

247
00:23:54.030 --> 00:23:55.532
I know your current situation.

248
00:23:57.043 --> 00:24:01.320
It's best that you stay
inside, close to where she is;

249
00:24:02.158 --> 00:24:03.159
Her energy.

250
00:24:06.393 --> 00:24:07.787
Why would you do that?

251
00:24:08.755 --> 00:24:10.857
I saw your story in the newspaper.

252
00:24:11.938 --> 00:24:14.113
I sense so much sadness in you.

253
00:24:15.321 --> 00:24:16.682
This is what I do.

254
00:24:16.683 --> 00:24:17.684
This is who I am.

255
00:24:21.739 --> 00:24:23.256
I don't know what to say.

256
00:24:24.421 --> 00:24:25.872
Say when to be there.

257
00:24:30.424 --> 00:24:31.887
Hey, that
therapist I told you about,

258
00:24:31.888 --> 00:24:34.780
she's willing to come out
and do few sessions for free.

259
00:24:34.781 --> 00:24:36.221
Really?

260
00:24:36.222 --> 00:24:37.223
Why?

261
00:24:38.264 --> 00:24:39.685
She wants to help.

262
00:24:39.686 --> 00:24:41.615
You know anything about her?

263
00:24:41.616 --> 00:24:43.959
Terry recommended her.

264
00:24:43.960 --> 00:24:45.247
Terry from work?

265
00:24:45.248 --> 00:24:46.892
Hm.

266
00:24:46.893 --> 00:24:47.726
You don't think it's weird,

267
00:24:47.727 --> 00:24:49.589
her coming out here and doing it for free?

268
00:24:51.615 --> 00:24:53.452
I got a good feeling about her.

269
00:24:55.722 --> 00:24:57.223
Why are you so high on this?

270
00:25:07.741 --> 00:25:12.746
Lately, I am having trouble
seeing a purpose in anything.

271
00:25:13.160 --> 00:25:15.273
Oh, babe, come on.

272
00:25:18.745 --> 00:25:21.665
What about coaching softball again?

273
00:25:22.586 --> 00:25:24.450
What does that have to do with anything?

274
00:25:24.451 --> 00:25:26.902
I'm just saying, I
mean it might help you

275
00:25:26.903 --> 00:25:28.944
find your purpose again.

276
00:25:28.945 --> 00:25:31.210
No, no, like a valid purpose for me.

277
00:25:32.048 --> 00:25:33.049
Nothing has purpose.

278
00:25:35.620 --> 00:25:38.207
What about all those cards
in there from your patients?

279
00:25:39.075 --> 00:25:40.376
Is there no purpose there?

280
00:25:42.168 --> 00:25:44.134
I can't help them anymore.

281
00:25:44.135 --> 00:25:46.387
- I'm a mess.
- Oh, come here.

282
00:25:48.749 --> 00:25:52.085
I have no reason to be anymore.

283
00:25:56.501 --> 00:25:58.335
What are you saying?

284
00:26:00.861 --> 00:26:01.694
Hm?

285
00:26:01.695 --> 00:26:03.216
Are you saying you'd rather be dead?

286
00:26:04.871 --> 00:26:05.872
No.

287
00:26:08.181 --> 00:26:09.182
Relax.

288
00:26:10.871 --> 00:26:13.275
I'm not.

289
00:26:13.276 --> 00:26:15.164
I'm just being dramatic.

290
00:26:16.685 --> 00:26:17.836
I'm sorry to upset you.

291
00:26:20.026 --> 00:26:21.027
Ally.

292
00:26:24.410 --> 00:26:25.712
So, what do I do?

293
00:26:27.313 --> 00:26:28.715
Strengthen the connection.

294
00:26:31.528 --> 00:26:32.879
Why do you want to see her?

295
00:26:35.772 --> 00:26:38.725
It's perfectly natural to want
to see our loved ones again.

296
00:26:40.637 --> 00:26:42.337
You've shown me you'd do anything to share

297
00:26:42.338 --> 00:26:43.540
another moment with her.

298
00:26:46.673 --> 00:26:50.069
The way you live, torturing yourself.

299
00:26:51.608 --> 00:26:53.462
Is that motivation driven by guilt?

300
00:26:54.420 --> 00:26:56.405
Do you feel somehow responsible?

301
00:27:03.499 --> 00:27:04.601
She had mood swings.

302
00:27:05.832 --> 00:27:08.384
And at first I thought it
was normal teenage angst.

303
00:27:09.525 --> 00:27:11.030
You talked to her about it?

304
00:27:12.515 --> 00:27:13.516
I tried.

305
00:27:15.201 --> 00:27:17.066
But it got bad really fast.

306
00:27:19.495 --> 00:27:23.412
In the last two weeks, she was really off.

307
00:27:25.051 --> 00:27:26.052
Up and down.

308
00:27:27.904 --> 00:27:32.552
And sometimes she was really scared.

309
00:27:33.549 --> 00:27:36.402
I just wish I had done something
the first time I saw it.

310
00:27:39.836 --> 00:27:41.641
So, yeah, I do feel responsible.

311
00:28:01.357 --> 00:28:02.959
Why don't you leave the house?

312
00:28:04.635 --> 00:28:05.636
I can't.

313
00:28:07.513 --> 00:28:08.514
Why?

314
00:28:13.159 --> 00:28:14.210
Because I'm scared.

315
00:28:19.235 --> 00:28:21.037
When I walk outside I can't breathe.

316
00:28:24.881 --> 00:28:28.624
The idea of doing normal
things like driving in a car

317
00:28:28.625 --> 00:28:32.371
or going to a friend's barbecue,

318
00:28:34.671 --> 00:28:39.676
working at a job, it's terrifying.

319
00:28:53.870 --> 00:28:55.371
Now we're getting somewhere.

320
00:28:57.153 --> 00:29:01.290
Everything you just said
is completely normal.

321
00:29:05.495 --> 00:29:06.582
No, it's nuts.

322
00:29:08.634 --> 00:29:09.829
We are therapists.

323
00:29:11.017 --> 00:29:12.742
Nuts are our specialty.

324
00:29:16.642 --> 00:29:19.833
Samantha was an artist
and she kept a sketchbook.

325
00:29:19.834 --> 00:29:21.086
I think I mentioned it on the phone.

326
00:29:21.087 --> 00:29:24.622
I think she was drawing
pictures of the scary things

327
00:29:24.623 --> 00:29:26.322
that she was seeing.

328
00:29:27.370 --> 00:29:29.853
And I am seeing the same things.

329
00:29:32.066 --> 00:29:33.067
May I see?

330
00:29:37.727 --> 00:29:39.156
This one.

331
00:29:39.157 --> 00:29:40.408
You saw this?

332
00:29:41.338 --> 00:29:45.355
Right out there just like it's drawn.

333
00:29:52.688 --> 00:29:53.777
Freaky stuff, right?

334
00:29:55.671 --> 00:29:56.722
You saw all of these?

335
00:29:56.723 --> 00:30:00.873
No, but the day Samantha
died she talked about a face,

336
00:30:00.874 --> 00:30:03.076
and it really scared the hell out of her.

337
00:30:05.071 --> 00:30:06.395
It's all very strange.

338
00:30:08.755 --> 00:30:12.621
Reminds me a story I heard, long ago.

339
00:30:17.433 --> 00:30:18.484
That's all for today.

340
00:30:24.700 --> 00:30:26.285
Strengthen the connection.

341
00:30:33.840 --> 00:30:34.841
Talk to me, Sam.

342
00:31:03.069 --> 00:31:06.111
Someone made a mistake
and put this in my hand.

343
00:31:06.112 --> 00:31:07.366
Get that outta here.

344
00:31:08.404 --> 00:31:11.636
Show me your uh,
your beautiful artwork here.

345
00:31:11.637 --> 00:31:13.539
Oh, you're a comedian, huh?

346
00:31:13.540 --> 00:31:14.930
- Dad!
- Hi, baby.

347
00:31:14.931 --> 00:31:16.885
- Hey.
- Be careful.

348
00:31:16.886 --> 00:31:18.403
Look at how soft it is.

349
00:31:18.404 --> 00:31:20.897
She's so cute, I don't
know where she gets it from.

350
00:31:20.898 --> 00:31:22.457
Aw.

351
00:31:22.458 --> 00:31:24.900
Ladies and gentlemen, what we have here

352
00:31:24.901 --> 00:31:27.943
is a grill full of hamburgers.

353
00:31:27.944 --> 00:31:29.618
There we go, that's
that famous Larkin wit.

354
00:31:29.619 --> 00:31:33.054
- Soon to be cheeseburgers.
- Mm.

355
00:31:33.055 --> 00:31:34.319
Be careful, you don't
want me to bust out my lines

356
00:31:34.320 --> 00:31:35.630
from the wedding now, do you?

357
00:31:35.631 --> 00:31:36.952
Oh, please.

358
00:31:36.953 --> 00:31:41.246
You know I love your "love
is baseball" metaphors.

359
00:31:41.247 --> 00:31:44.000
Blah!

360
00:31:45.024 --> 00:31:45.857
Don't.

361
00:31:45.858 --> 00:31:47.182
Get the camera outta my face.

362
00:31:47.183 --> 00:31:49.855
Samantha, can you come over here?

363
00:31:49.856 --> 00:31:51.907
Can I take a video of you?

364
00:31:51.908 --> 00:31:52.740
- Yeah.
- Come here.

365
00:31:52.741 --> 00:31:54.089
All right, pause right there.

366
00:31:54.090 --> 00:31:56.161
Can you say, "I'm four years old."

367
00:31:56.162 --> 00:31:57.777
I'm four years old.

368
00:31:57.778 --> 00:31:58.952
And I'm almost a grownup.

369
00:31:58.953 --> 00:32:01.045
I'm almost a grownup.

370
00:32:01.046 --> 00:32:02.737
And I can take care of myself.

371
00:32:02.738 --> 00:32:05.190
I can take care of myself.

372
00:32:05.191 --> 00:32:06.746
That's good.

373
00:32:43.745 --> 00:32:45.241
Hi.

374
00:32:45.242 --> 00:32:47.077
How'd you get in here?

375
00:32:50.253 --> 00:32:51.254
Are you lost?

376
00:32:54.532 --> 00:32:55.412
You're not in trouble.

377
00:32:55.413 --> 00:32:56.246
It's okay.

378
00:32:56.247 --> 00:32:58.267
I just need you to talk to me.

379
00:33:40.713 --> 00:33:44.384
Were you watching home
movies in Sam's room?

380
00:33:45.271 --> 00:33:46.272
No.

381
00:33:47.183 --> 00:33:48.184
Why?

382
00:33:48.965 --> 00:33:50.466
There was a tape in the VCR.

383
00:33:53.809 --> 00:33:55.361
So maybe she was watching it?

384
00:34:03.219 --> 00:34:07.002
There's nothing we coulda done, right?

385
00:34:07.003 --> 00:34:08.004
Right.

386
00:34:12.969 --> 00:34:14.712
Must've been a warning sign.

387
00:34:14.713 --> 00:34:16.031
I just wish I had seen it.

388
00:34:16.032 --> 00:34:17.283
So maybe you missed it.

389
00:34:19.505 --> 00:34:21.057
Nothing we can do about it now.

390
00:34:23.579 --> 00:34:25.524
So that means I'm terrible at my job.

391
00:34:29.895 --> 00:34:31.186
A little reassurance would be nice.

392
00:34:31.187 --> 00:34:32.511
What do you want me to say?

393
00:34:33.899 --> 00:34:36.381
She saw things that weren't real.

394
00:34:36.382 --> 00:34:37.383
That's your fault?

395
00:34:38.772 --> 00:34:40.124
I shoulda done something.

396
00:34:42.338 --> 00:34:43.922
What about you the other night?

397
00:34:45.061 --> 00:34:46.831
There's no purpose in anything.

398
00:34:46.832 --> 00:34:48.643
Is that a warning sign?

399
00:34:48.644 --> 00:34:50.165
Should I be doing something?

400
00:34:50.166 --> 00:34:51.426
You think I'm ridiculous?

401
00:34:51.427 --> 00:34:53.508
No, no, I never said that.

402
00:34:53.509 --> 00:34:55.300
I told you years ago I
would never use that word

403
00:34:55.301 --> 00:34:56.851
to describe someone.

404
00:34:56.852 --> 00:34:58.174
We're human beings.

405
00:34:58.175 --> 00:34:59.176
We do what we do.

406
00:35:02.996 --> 00:35:04.748
I don't know what to say sometimes.

407
00:35:05.981 --> 00:35:07.823
You had a few words worth moments.

408
00:35:11.404 --> 00:35:14.107
Nah, I just think you like
my old cheese ball lines.

409
00:35:15.061 --> 00:35:17.722
Remember what you said
to me on our wedding day?

410
00:35:17.723 --> 00:35:18.724
Oh, yeah.

411
00:35:19.695 --> 00:35:23.468
Was it uh, "I've always
swung for the fences",

412
00:35:23.469 --> 00:35:25.878
but with you I actually connected."

413
00:35:27.580 --> 00:35:29.058
Wow, no stumping you.

414
00:35:31.084 --> 00:35:32.085
Yeah.

415
00:35:33.028 --> 00:35:34.493
Never got that cabin.

416
00:35:36.042 --> 00:35:37.106
You have to remind me?

417
00:35:40.546 --> 00:35:41.760
Cool mountain air.

418
00:35:43.799 --> 00:35:46.152
We once said that was
the epitome of happiness.

419
00:35:54.450 --> 00:35:55.901
Think it's too late for us?

420
00:35:58.105 --> 00:35:59.189
I hope not.

421
00:36:06.762 --> 00:36:08.553
Remember that dance at our wedding?

422
00:36:08.554 --> 00:36:10.977
And I did this and this.

423
00:36:13.389 --> 00:36:16.058
Good moves, Mr. Larkin.

424
00:36:17.233 --> 00:36:18.303
How much longer do you think

425
00:36:18.304 --> 00:36:19.818
he'll humor your reclusiveness?

426
00:36:21.790 --> 00:36:23.142
As long as it takes.

427
00:36:24.690 --> 00:36:26.192
How long will that be?

428
00:36:27.033 --> 00:36:28.034
I don't know.

429
00:36:29.054 --> 00:36:32.010
But he's been very supportive
and he still cares.

430
00:36:33.729 --> 00:36:35.704
He goes to work everyday,

431
00:36:36.802 --> 00:36:39.405
takes on all the financial
burden without complaint.

432
00:36:40.836 --> 00:36:42.161
What are you trying to say?

433
00:36:43.495 --> 00:36:45.574
Are you sure he's at
work the whole time?

434
00:36:46.802 --> 00:36:48.404
You think he's cheating on me?

435
00:36:49.869 --> 00:36:51.416
It's just a thought.

436
00:36:51.417 --> 00:36:53.358
Here's a thought, Jan.

437
00:36:53.359 --> 00:36:55.110
Why don't you blow it out your ass?

438
00:37:01.837 --> 00:37:02.838
Touche.

439
00:37:05.591 --> 00:37:07.986
There's something I've been
wanting to talk to you about.

440
00:37:09.545 --> 00:37:10.646
Samantha's sketchbook.

441
00:37:12.168 --> 00:37:13.169
Yeah.

442
00:37:14.125 --> 00:37:15.480
I was gonna actually bring that up.

443
00:37:15.481 --> 00:37:17.356
It seemed like it kind of upset you.

444
00:37:18.750 --> 00:37:20.452
I was hesitant to talk about it.

445
00:37:22.007 --> 00:37:23.522
I heard a ghost story once.

446
00:37:25.020 --> 00:37:28.283
About a scarred face with no eyes.

447
00:37:28.284 --> 00:37:29.511
You've heard the saying,

448
00:37:29.512 --> 00:37:32.350
"The eyes are the window to the soul?"

449
00:37:32.351 --> 00:37:33.602
Mm hm.

450
00:37:34.970 --> 00:37:37.856
Many years ago I was a
missionary in Botswana.

451
00:37:39.665 --> 00:37:42.877
The locals told us about the Ubuso.

452
00:37:42.878 --> 00:37:46.971
A malevolent shape shifting
spirit from an ancient world.

453
00:37:46.972 --> 00:37:50.855
On its own it was simply
the air you breathe,

454
00:37:50.856 --> 00:37:54.583
but to its victims it was
the embodiment of insanity.

455
00:37:55.891 --> 00:37:58.657
The Ubuso had no eyes in its true form.

456
00:37:59.565 --> 00:38:01.876
It would steal eyes from humans

457
00:38:01.877 --> 00:38:04.839
and use their eyes to see into their soul.

458
00:38:04.840 --> 00:38:07.526
To find their will to live and destroy it.

459
00:38:09.439 --> 00:38:11.566
The Ubuso fed on misery.

460
00:38:11.567 --> 00:38:13.432
So, if it would see into your soul,

461
00:38:14.274 --> 00:38:18.327
it could see your fears,
your sadness, your pain.

462
00:38:19.415 --> 00:38:21.334
How did they stop it?

463
00:38:23.335 --> 00:38:24.503
They didn't.

464
00:38:26.402 --> 00:38:30.014
In the Zulu language,
Ubuso means many faces.

465
00:38:30.015 --> 00:38:32.126
The spirit had the ability
to take on any form.

466
00:38:32.127 --> 00:38:33.918
That's how it got its name.

467
00:38:33.919 --> 00:38:37.105
Once it burrowed deep
into a person's psyche,

468
00:38:38.003 --> 00:38:39.678
it could manipulate reality.

469
00:38:41.206 --> 00:38:44.012
Once that happened, madness set in.

470
00:38:45.408 --> 00:38:46.409
And led to suicide.

471
00:38:47.523 --> 00:38:49.354
The spirit was a parasite,

472
00:38:49.355 --> 00:38:52.511
so afterward it moved on to another.

473
00:38:54.297 --> 00:38:55.898
And this is what happened to Samantha?

474
00:38:57.047 --> 00:38:58.048
And me?

475
00:38:59.646 --> 00:39:03.332
No, it's just a story.

476
00:39:04.950 --> 00:39:07.155
The drawings are just a wild coincidence.

477
00:39:09.685 --> 00:39:11.450
So, why are you telling me this?

478
00:39:13.018 --> 00:39:16.194
Stories are created to
explain the unexplainable.

479
00:39:20.796 --> 00:39:22.150
You want to know why.

480
00:39:24.009 --> 00:39:26.665
I believe Samantha is trying to show you.

481
00:39:29.958 --> 00:39:32.026
So I can understand
what she went through.

482
00:39:32.027 --> 00:39:33.028
Yes.

483
00:39:34.630 --> 00:39:37.662
We need to continue to
build the connection.

484
00:39:37.663 --> 00:39:38.864
Keep drinking the tea.

485
00:39:40.306 --> 00:39:42.958
The door's already open,
you don't need to do that.

486
00:39:44.039 --> 00:39:46.034
You're not still drinking it are you?

487
00:39:54.700 --> 00:39:56.721
What I've seen, it's not just vision.

488
00:39:56.722 --> 00:39:58.474
It's trying to communicate with me.

489
00:39:59.815 --> 00:40:01.016
How do you mean?

490
00:40:02.027 --> 00:40:05.720
I saw a boy in Samantha's room.

491
00:40:05.721 --> 00:40:06.765
He had no mouth.

492
00:40:07.683 --> 00:40:09.708
And I saw him in Samantha's sketchbook.

493
00:40:10.766 --> 00:40:12.267
Samantha's breaking through.

494
00:40:14.850 --> 00:40:19.221
He wrote on the wall,
"Give me your voice."

495
00:40:20.826 --> 00:40:22.270
So it's gotta be connected.

496
00:40:23.899 --> 00:40:25.093
Don't think so much.

497
00:40:26.832 --> 00:40:30.549
When you see Samantha,
it will all make sense.

498
00:40:31.907 --> 00:40:33.598
Seems like I'm gonna
have to see the face

499
00:40:33.599 --> 00:40:35.283
with no eyes before that happens.

500
00:40:36.752 --> 00:40:37.903
Let's hope you don't.

501
00:40:41.957 --> 00:40:42.958
Hey.

502
00:40:45.050 --> 00:40:46.751
Can I talk to you about something?

503
00:40:46.752 --> 00:40:48.653
Sure.

504
00:40:48.654 --> 00:40:49.655
Sit down.

505
00:40:59.715 --> 00:41:01.517
We were just kids when Sam was born.

506
00:41:02.488 --> 00:41:05.276
We talked about having another
baby when things settled down

507
00:41:05.277 --> 00:41:06.455
and we finished school.

508
00:41:07.973 --> 00:41:09.812
We never had that conversation.

509
00:41:10.966 --> 00:41:11.967
Yeah.

510
00:41:13.839 --> 00:41:14.840
Life happened.

511
00:41:17.222 --> 00:41:18.223
Yeah.

512
00:41:19.264 --> 00:41:21.216
You wanna have that conversation now?

513
00:41:25.643 --> 00:41:27.091
Why?

514
00:41:27.092 --> 00:41:28.093
Why not?

515
00:41:29.187 --> 00:41:33.107
Why now?

516
00:41:33.108 --> 00:41:34.859
- You wanna replace Sam?
- No.

517
00:41:34.860 --> 00:41:38.332
No, no, baby, no, no, I did not say that.

518
00:41:38.333 --> 00:41:40.779
Please don't put words in my mouth.

519
00:41:43.138 --> 00:41:44.409
So, why then?

520
00:41:44.410 --> 00:41:45.740
I'm just merely bringing up the fact

521
00:41:45.741 --> 00:41:47.493
that we never had the conversation.

522
00:41:52.037 --> 00:41:54.739
- We're not ready for that.
- We're not ready?

523
00:41:54.740 --> 00:41:56.921
Okay, I'm not ready.

524
00:41:56.922 --> 00:41:58.853
Don't do that, don't
blow me off every time

525
00:41:58.854 --> 00:42:01.315
I try to have a real
conversation about something.

526
00:42:01.316 --> 00:42:03.367
You always storm off.

527
00:42:03.368 --> 00:42:05.139
It's ridiculous.

528
00:42:05.140 --> 00:42:06.080
I'm ridiculous?

529
00:42:06.081 --> 00:42:09.043
No, I said this is
ridiculous, this situation.

530
00:42:09.044 --> 00:42:11.697
I already told you I would
never call you ridiculous.

531
00:42:32.137 --> 00:42:33.556
Mom?

532
00:42:56.562 --> 00:42:57.563
Hello?

533
00:43:01.907 --> 00:43:02.908
Samantha?

534
00:43:15.404 --> 00:43:18.407
Are you trying to tell me something?

535
00:43:21.186 --> 00:43:23.772
If you are, I don't understand.

536
00:43:35.647 --> 00:43:37.149
Mom?

537
00:43:39.729 --> 00:43:41.986
Why didn't you stop me?

538
00:43:44.906 --> 00:43:46.240
Look what I did.

539
00:43:51.093 --> 00:43:53.178
This isn't real.

540
00:44:14.076 --> 00:44:15.460
Come outside, Mom.

541
00:44:15.461 --> 00:44:17.463
The weather's fantastic.

542
00:44:31.670 --> 00:44:33.541
Healing is not without pain.

543
00:44:36.822 --> 00:44:38.392
We have to look at ourselves in the mirror

544
00:44:38.393 --> 00:44:39.497
and see the truth.

545
00:44:40.455 --> 00:44:41.445
I've seen plenty of things.

546
00:44:41.446 --> 00:44:43.277
There's no truth to any of it.

547
00:44:43.278 --> 00:44:44.930
It's part of the process.

548
00:44:47.189 --> 00:44:48.962
I can barely will myself
out of bed every morning,

549
00:44:48.963 --> 00:44:51.756
and then you came along and
everything's the same except

550
00:44:51.757 --> 00:44:54.708
for now I don't know what's real.

551
00:44:54.709 --> 00:44:55.710
Mom?

552
00:45:01.937 --> 00:45:02.938
Do you hear that?

553
00:45:05.360 --> 00:45:07.616
You're still
drinking the tea aren't you?

554
00:45:08.504 --> 00:45:10.635
I don't see anything without it.

555
00:45:10.636 --> 00:45:12.767
That's not how it works.

556
00:45:12.768 --> 00:45:13.948
Dump it down the drain.

557
00:45:13.949 --> 00:45:17.011
It's done, you can already
see the other side.

558
00:45:17.012 --> 00:45:18.013
Is that so?

559
00:45:19.004 --> 00:45:20.795
How many awful things
did you have to endure

560
00:45:20.796 --> 00:45:22.347
before you got to see your son?

561
00:45:23.288 --> 00:45:24.289
Patience.

562
00:45:25.160 --> 00:45:27.062
You told me to take a leap of faith.

563
00:45:28.340 --> 00:45:29.341
I did.

564
00:45:31.700 --> 00:45:33.561
When do I get to see my daughter?

565
00:45:34.479 --> 00:45:36.136
You're not there yet.

566
00:45:36.137 --> 00:45:37.138
When then?

567
00:45:38.427 --> 00:45:40.079
When I've gone completely insane?

568
00:45:42.337 --> 00:45:44.028
Insane people don't have the wherewithal

569
00:45:44.029 --> 00:45:45.924
to acknowledge their own insanity.

570
00:45:49.805 --> 00:45:53.862
I saw my daughter's dead body
come alive in the bath tub.

571
00:45:57.773 --> 00:46:01.495
What does that do to help me
understand her or her illness?

572
00:46:01.496 --> 00:46:03.407
Ally, it's not that simple.

573
00:46:03.408 --> 00:46:05.579
Perhaps she's waiting for
you to sort something out

574
00:46:05.580 --> 00:46:06.646
with her father.

575
00:46:06.647 --> 00:46:08.449
Like what?

576
00:46:08.450 --> 00:46:11.115
Do you know where
Michael stands with you?

577
00:46:11.116 --> 00:46:12.117
With your family?

578
00:46:13.729 --> 00:46:15.063
He wants to have a baby.

579
00:46:16.772 --> 00:46:17.773
Really?

580
00:46:19.394 --> 00:46:21.445
A replacement for Samantha?

581
00:46:21.446 --> 00:46:23.101
No, not like that.

582
00:46:26.732 --> 00:46:29.097
- How old are you?
- 36.

583
00:46:30.806 --> 00:46:31.807
Why?

584
00:46:33.358 --> 00:46:34.989
You don't have much time left.

585
00:46:34.990 --> 00:46:35.991
For what?

586
00:46:37.699 --> 00:46:38.950
To have a family again.

587
00:46:40.605 --> 00:46:42.546
Time is limited for Michael as well.

588
00:46:42.547 --> 00:46:45.699
If this is what he wants,
he might consider starting

589
00:46:45.700 --> 00:46:47.065
a family with someone else.

590
00:46:48.029 --> 00:46:50.855
On what planet would
that be considered helpful?

591
00:46:50.856 --> 00:46:52.777
It's part of the process.

592
00:46:52.778 --> 00:46:53.918
Get out.

593
00:46:53.919 --> 00:46:54.920
Ally.

594
00:46:57.058 --> 00:46:59.113
I don't like the way I
feel when I'm with you.

595
00:46:59.114 --> 00:47:01.967
You knew that I would
push you to talk, remember?

596
00:47:03.668 --> 00:47:08.673
I've decided that
drugs and ghost stories

597
00:47:09.024 --> 00:47:10.168
are not good therapy.

598
00:47:12.087 --> 00:47:13.605
I don't mean to offend.

599
00:47:13.606 --> 00:47:15.108
I'm not gonna ask you again.

600
00:48:02.858 --> 00:48:04.132
Michael, are you home?

601
00:48:17.632 --> 00:48:19.661
Jesus, kid, enough with the jump scares.

602
00:48:28.791 --> 00:48:30.210
What do you want?

603
00:48:55.096 --> 00:48:57.804
Why do you torture me with memories?

604
00:49:59.829 --> 00:50:00.830
Samantha?

605
00:50:04.895 --> 00:50:05.896
Mornin'.

606
00:50:11.305 --> 00:50:13.437
Am I dreaming?

607
00:50:13.438 --> 00:50:14.439
No.

608
00:50:15.730 --> 00:50:16.731
It's really me.

609
00:50:21.516 --> 00:50:23.327
I miss you so much.

610
00:50:23.328 --> 00:50:26.694
Mom, you need to listen to me.

611
00:50:28.614 --> 00:50:29.698
What is it?

612
00:50:30.662 --> 00:50:32.590
You're going down the same path.

613
00:50:36.201 --> 00:50:37.525
You're seeing what I saw.

614
00:50:39.932 --> 00:50:41.534
But you've yet to see the worst.

615
00:50:46.753 --> 00:50:48.005
It never stops.

616
00:50:51.737 --> 00:50:54.213
I'm so sorry, I didn't know.

617
00:50:54.214 --> 00:50:55.215
But you did know.

618
00:50:56.621 --> 00:50:57.622
I was sick.

619
00:51:03.658 --> 00:51:05.682
I've wished so many
times I could stop you

620
00:51:05.683 --> 00:51:08.432
from going in that garage.

621
00:51:08.433 --> 00:51:10.085
Stop making excuses.

622
00:51:13.148 --> 00:51:14.756
So you do blame me?

623
00:51:15.920 --> 00:51:17.722
Don't you wanna make things right?

624
00:51:21.028 --> 00:51:22.079
I don't understand.

625
00:51:23.142 --> 00:51:24.443
You've become a shut-in.

626
00:51:25.360 --> 00:51:30.365
Your career, your marriage,
your life is a joke.

627
00:51:32.587 --> 00:51:33.588
What?

628
00:51:34.957 --> 00:51:36.111
Why would you say that?

629
00:51:37.142 --> 00:51:39.597
You've nailed yourself to a cross.

630
00:51:40.442 --> 00:51:42.026
Why?

631
00:51:42.027 --> 00:51:43.921
To prove you were a good mother?

632
00:51:45.374 --> 00:51:46.964
You don't think I was a good mother?

633
00:51:54.951 --> 00:51:57.621
But you can make things right.

634
00:51:59.706 --> 00:52:00.707
End it.

635
00:52:02.380 --> 00:52:05.093
Give me your eyes.

636
00:52:07.112 --> 00:52:08.113
Your eyes.

637
00:52:08.883 --> 00:52:09.884
Give 'em to me.

638
00:52:17.243 --> 00:52:18.432
You're not real.

639
00:52:18.433 --> 00:52:20.535
Oh, am I real now?

640
00:52:25.869 --> 00:52:27.318
Some of 'em slit their wrists.

641
00:52:27.319 --> 00:52:29.447
Some of 'em put a gun in their mouth.

642
00:52:31.109 --> 00:52:32.360
You'll cut out your eyes.

643
00:52:34.466 --> 00:52:35.967
Just like she did.

644
00:52:37.330 --> 00:52:38.581
Just like this.

645
00:52:41.409 --> 00:52:42.609
Ally, what's wrong?

646
00:52:42.610 --> 00:52:47.146
What happened?

647
00:52:47.147 --> 00:52:49.444
What happened, babe?

648
00:52:49.445 --> 00:52:51.890
You just walked into the
kitchen and started screaming.

649
00:52:51.891 --> 00:52:52.724
What the hell's going on?

650
00:52:52.725 --> 00:52:54.972
- I thought I saw Sam.
- You, whoa, whoa, whoa.

651
00:52:54.973 --> 00:52:55.929
But it wasn't her.

652
00:52:55.930 --> 00:52:57.532
You thought you saw Sam again?

653
00:52:58.761 --> 00:53:00.355
That's it, I'm taking you to a doctor.

654
00:53:00.356 --> 00:53:01.875
No.

655
00:53:01.876 --> 00:53:03.056
I'm not gonna sit back and watch you

656
00:53:03.057 --> 00:53:04.765
keep doing this to yourself.

657
00:53:07.265 --> 00:53:08.098
If you won't leave the house,

658
00:53:08.099 --> 00:53:09.854
I'm gonna call one and bring one here.

659
00:53:10.695 --> 00:53:12.547
I'm sorry, but this is nonnegotiable.

660
00:53:21.926 --> 00:53:23.777
Physically you're fine.

661
00:53:23.778 --> 00:53:25.693
- It's just stress.
- That's it?

662
00:53:26.531 --> 00:53:29.493
With a traumatic event like
you've both been through,

663
00:53:29.494 --> 00:53:30.645
it's perfectly natural.

664
00:53:32.446 --> 00:53:34.856
Are you taking any medications currently?

665
00:53:34.857 --> 00:53:35.796
I take a Valium sometimes.

666
00:53:35.797 --> 00:53:37.931
- You take that with alcohol?
- She hasn't had anything

667
00:53:37.932 --> 00:53:39.153
to drink today.

668
00:53:39.154 --> 00:53:41.606
Michael, this is
embarrassing enough as it is.

669
00:53:41.607 --> 00:53:42.958
He doesn't need to be here.

670
00:53:44.078 --> 00:53:46.320
Well, I brought some
samples 'cause I thought

671
00:53:46.321 --> 00:53:47.445
they'd come in handy.

672
00:53:48.543 --> 00:53:50.345
And I will write you a prescription.

673
00:53:55.360 --> 00:53:56.670
Take one of those once a day.

674
00:53:56.671 --> 00:53:58.826
Only those, no other pills, no booze.

675
00:53:59.694 --> 00:54:00.586
What is it?

676
00:54:00.587 --> 00:54:01.420
It's a strong sedative.

677
00:54:01.421 --> 00:54:03.671
- It'll keep you calm.
- And then what?

678
00:54:05.974 --> 00:54:08.699
The elephant in the room, the visions.

679
00:54:08.700 --> 00:54:09.983
I need to run some tests.

680
00:54:09.984 --> 00:54:11.735
An MRI is a good start.

681
00:54:11.736 --> 00:54:13.267
- I don't need an MRI.
- Ally.

682
00:54:13.268 --> 00:54:14.508
I'm not stressed.

683
00:54:14.509 --> 00:54:15.342
I'm not crazy.

684
00:54:15.343 --> 00:54:16.910
I'm not having a nervous breakdown.

685
00:54:16.911 --> 00:54:18.612
It was all a hallucination.

686
00:54:18.613 --> 00:54:20.664
I've been drinking a
tea that had this stuff

687
00:54:20.665 --> 00:54:21.666
called Datura in it.

688
00:54:22.587 --> 00:54:23.617
Datura?

689
00:54:23.618 --> 00:54:24.989
Well, that's Jimsonweed.

690
00:54:26.024 --> 00:54:28.222
I don't know, sure.

691
00:54:28.223 --> 00:54:30.864
Okay, can somebody fill me in?

692
00:54:30.865 --> 00:54:32.466
It's a drug that makes you see things.

693
00:54:32.467 --> 00:54:33.521
It's poison.

694
00:54:34.429 --> 00:54:36.741
We may need to get her to the ER.

695
00:54:36.742 --> 00:54:39.077
No, I'm not on it anymore.

696
00:54:39.944 --> 00:54:41.205
I swear.

697
00:54:41.206 --> 00:54:42.226
It will kill you.

698
00:54:42.227 --> 00:54:43.278
You know that, right?

699
00:54:44.339 --> 00:54:45.439
How much?

700
00:54:45.440 --> 00:54:46.273
How much what?

701
00:54:46.274 --> 00:54:47.106
Would kill you?

702
00:54:47.107 --> 00:54:48.322
Any amount, the smallest amount.

703
00:54:48.323 --> 00:54:50.904
Please do not take this lightly.

704
00:54:50.905 --> 00:54:52.926
This is not magic mushrooms
where you get a case

705
00:54:52.927 --> 00:54:55.339
of the giggles while
watching the carpet breathe.

706
00:54:55.340 --> 00:54:57.120
Datura is something else entirely.

707
00:54:57.121 --> 00:55:00.394
It's having conversations
with people that don't exist.

708
00:55:00.395 --> 00:55:03.176
Assuming you don't die,
it's self-induced insanity.

709
00:55:03.177 --> 00:55:04.278
Ally.

710
00:55:04.279 --> 00:55:05.839
The therapist, she gave it to me.

711
00:55:05.840 --> 00:55:07.725
The lady making the house calls?

712
00:55:08.683 --> 00:55:11.062
I knew something was up with that quack.

713
00:55:11.063 --> 00:55:12.525
Do you still have this drug?

714
00:55:12.526 --> 00:55:16.099
Yeah.

715
00:55:16.100 --> 00:55:17.271
It is all a stupid mistake.

716
00:55:17.272 --> 00:55:18.782
I'm getting it right now.

717
00:55:18.783 --> 00:55:20.394
Please take it out of my hands.

718
00:55:20.395 --> 00:55:22.346
This is all a disaster, really.

719
00:55:22.347 --> 00:55:23.627
The therapist that gave it to you,

720
00:55:23.628 --> 00:55:25.829
do you have their contact information?

721
00:55:25.830 --> 00:55:28.396
Yes, I'll get you her card.

722
00:55:30.485 --> 00:55:31.415
No wonder she'd feel the effects

723
00:55:31.416 --> 00:55:32.417
if it was a drug.

724
00:55:33.758 --> 00:55:35.023
Under the influence it's impossible

725
00:55:35.024 --> 00:55:36.576
to decern fantasy from reality.

726
00:55:37.872 --> 00:55:40.508
Your daughter, she saw things too?

727
00:55:42.056 --> 00:55:44.598
Yeah, but it wasn't drugs.

728
00:55:44.599 --> 00:55:46.270
We had an autopsy done.

729
00:55:46.271 --> 00:55:47.911
Does mental illness run in the family?

730
00:55:47.912 --> 00:55:49.142
- No.
- Schizophrenia?

731
00:55:49.143 --> 00:55:51.435
No, no, nothing like that.

732
00:55:51.436 --> 00:55:55.539
Um, but listen, this has been
going on for a while now.

733
00:55:55.540 --> 00:55:58.065
She won't leave the house, ever.

734
00:55:59.574 --> 00:56:00.775
I think she's losing it.

735
00:56:02.827 --> 00:56:04.983
I think she's causing me to lose it, too.

736
00:56:04.984 --> 00:56:06.986
I can't find her card.

737
00:56:08.993 --> 00:56:12.165
Her name is Janice Rollins,
I'll find her number later.

738
00:56:12.166 --> 00:56:14.097
It's fine, I can
probably dig up some info

739
00:56:14.098 --> 00:56:14.931
just based on the name.

740
00:56:14.932 --> 00:56:16.420
Why would you do something like this?

741
00:56:16.421 --> 00:56:19.313
You're in the medical field,
you should know better.

742
00:56:19.314 --> 00:56:22.105
She told me I could
see my daughter again.

743
00:56:22.106 --> 00:56:23.207
What does that mean?

744
00:56:24.048 --> 00:56:26.089
Sam's ghost, I could talk
to her on the other side.

745
00:56:26.090 --> 00:56:27.542
Oh, Jesus Christ.

746
00:56:31.336 --> 00:56:32.906
What's in this stuff?

747
00:56:32.907 --> 00:56:34.948
It's strong, like I said.

748
00:56:34.949 --> 00:56:36.259
Just get some rest.

749
00:56:36.260 --> 00:56:38.513
You need to get this
stuff outta your system.

750
00:56:39.764 --> 00:56:41.776
Let me borrow you for a second.

751
00:56:43.918 --> 00:56:44.751
You gotta do something.

752
00:56:44.752 --> 00:56:46.883
Yeah, I'm gonna do some tests for me,

753
00:56:46.884 --> 00:56:49.078
we'll get this sorted out.

754
00:56:49.079 --> 00:56:51.004
What kinda stuff are you worried about?

755
00:57:48.411 --> 00:57:49.412
Ally?

756
00:57:50.613 --> 00:57:53.699
How long have I been asleep?

757
00:57:56.271 --> 00:57:57.272
18 hours.

758
00:58:06.974 --> 00:58:08.335
It's okay, you needed it.

759
00:58:10.245 --> 00:58:13.248
The doctor said that stuff can
stay in your system for days.

760
00:58:18.142 --> 00:58:19.973
Why aren't you at work?

761
00:58:19.974 --> 00:58:22.015
I'm taking a few days off.

762
00:58:22.016 --> 00:58:23.100
Why?

763
00:58:26.250 --> 00:58:27.702
I wanna keep an eye on you.

764
00:58:29.474 --> 00:58:32.148
Sweetie, you don't need to do that.

765
00:58:32.149 --> 00:58:36.202
I know I've been a mess, but
I don't need a babysitter.

766
00:58:36.203 --> 00:58:37.204
It's okay.

767
00:58:38.713 --> 00:58:39.714
I wanna be here.

768
00:58:42.835 --> 00:58:44.687
That was pretty scary shit, you know?

769
00:58:46.690 --> 00:58:48.542
I'm gonna make it right, I promise.

770
00:58:49.641 --> 00:58:51.064
I shoulda known something
was up the other day

771
00:58:51.065 --> 00:58:53.518
when you thought you saw
someone in the backyard.

772
00:58:56.480 --> 00:58:59.432
I mean, why would you
do something like that?

773
00:58:59.433 --> 00:59:01.358
Take a drug from a complete stranger?

774
00:59:03.216 --> 00:59:05.759
I wanted to see Samantha so
bad, I had nothing to lose.

775
00:59:05.760 --> 00:59:07.360
I was ready to die.

776
00:59:07.361 --> 00:59:09.092
So the other night when you said

777
00:59:09.093 --> 00:59:12.369
you were just being
dramatic, that was a lie?

778
00:59:14.826 --> 00:59:15.827
Yeah.

779
00:59:25.279 --> 00:59:26.561
I don't know what else to say.

780
00:59:33.721 --> 00:59:37.059
This is my wake-up call, sweetie.

781
00:59:37.060 --> 00:59:38.796
I'm so embarrassed.

782
00:59:38.797 --> 00:59:40.397
I drank poison from a stranger.

783
00:59:42.289 --> 00:59:43.396
I've been a walking disaster.

784
00:59:43.397 --> 00:59:44.566
It's not fair to you.

785
00:59:46.019 --> 00:59:48.474
And a string of bad decisions.

786
00:59:48.475 --> 00:59:49.977
I wanna do better.

787
00:59:51.790 --> 00:59:55.722
I'll make it right.

788
00:59:55.723 --> 00:59:56.724
How?

789
00:59:58.850 --> 01:00:00.101
I don't know.

790
01:00:03.450 --> 01:00:07.127
I feel like everything's gonna be okay.

791
01:00:09.685 --> 01:00:14.106
Once you hit rock bottom,
there's only one way to go.

792
01:00:37.068 --> 01:00:38.570
I've missed you.

793
01:01:10.245 --> 01:01:11.078
This is Jan Rollins.

794
01:01:11.079 --> 01:01:12.439
Leave me a message.

795
01:01:14.038 --> 01:01:16.090
Hey, Jan, what you did, I need answers.

796
01:01:31.848 --> 01:01:33.349
Feeling all right?

797
01:01:34.719 --> 01:01:36.270
What are you doing?

798
01:01:37.231 --> 01:01:38.232
Strategy.

799
01:01:39.190 --> 01:01:41.042
I'm gonna hit up all my old patients.

800
01:01:42.817 --> 01:01:43.818
Why?

801
01:01:45.579 --> 01:01:47.034
I'm gonna start my own practice.

802
01:01:50.735 --> 01:01:53.466
Are you sure you're ready
for something like that?

803
01:01:53.467 --> 01:01:54.468
Probably not.

804
01:01:55.479 --> 01:01:57.921
But I'll tell myself I am
as many times as I need to

805
01:01:57.922 --> 01:01:59.303
until I believe it.

806
01:02:01.468 --> 01:02:03.256
I'm too good to work for
a healthcare network.

807
01:02:03.257 --> 01:02:05.468
I should've broken off
on my own years ago,

808
01:02:05.469 --> 01:02:06.771
but I was just too scared.

809
01:02:08.461 --> 01:02:10.854
That's great.

810
01:02:10.855 --> 01:02:12.832
I got in this business to help people,

811
01:02:12.833 --> 01:02:14.134
and I wanna get that back.

812
01:02:16.020 --> 01:02:16.853
I don't wanna get ahead of myself,

813
01:02:16.854 --> 01:02:20.393
but I might take your suggestion

814
01:02:20.394 --> 01:02:22.740
and start coaching softball again.

815
01:02:25.469 --> 01:02:26.470
Wow.

816
01:02:32.797 --> 01:02:35.118
No booze?

817
01:02:35.119 --> 01:02:36.120
Baby steps.

818
01:02:38.562 --> 01:02:40.815
Baby steps would be
going outside for once.

819
01:02:44.759 --> 01:02:46.060
What's with you tonight?

820
01:02:49.593 --> 01:02:52.545
- Hello?
- Hi, Kate.

821
01:02:52.546 --> 01:02:53.547
Oh, my God.

822
01:02:54.658 --> 01:02:56.723
I'm sorry it's been a while.

823
01:02:56.724 --> 01:02:59.132
It is so good to hear from you.

824
01:02:59.133 --> 01:03:00.303
Are you okay?

825
01:03:00.304 --> 01:03:02.351
Yeah, no, I'm good.

826
01:03:02.352 --> 01:03:04.127
I remembered that postcard you gave me

827
01:03:04.128 --> 01:03:05.329
with the mountain scape.

828
01:03:06.557 --> 01:03:08.715
It really meant a lot to me, so thank you.

829
01:03:08.716 --> 01:03:09.743
Are you kidding?

830
01:03:09.744 --> 01:03:12.055
- Anytime.
- Thank you.

831
01:03:12.056 --> 01:03:15.258
Well, I'm gonna be starting
my own practice soon,

832
01:03:15.259 --> 01:03:18.972
and if you wanted to continue
our sessions we could do that.

833
01:03:18.973 --> 01:03:22.527
Maybe in a few weeks or
months even, when I'm settled.

834
01:03:22.528 --> 01:03:23.767
Really?

835
01:03:23.768 --> 01:03:26.329
Congrats, that's so exciting.

836
01:03:26.330 --> 01:03:27.560
Of course.

837
01:03:27.561 --> 01:03:28.930
I speak the world of you.

838
01:03:29.816 --> 01:03:31.261
Thank you.

839
01:03:31.262 --> 01:03:32.459
I'm to the moon, Kate.

840
01:03:33.948 --> 01:03:35.249
I guess we'll be in touch.

841
01:03:36.195 --> 01:03:37.196
Okay, bye.

842
01:03:56.570 --> 01:03:57.571
- Hello?
- Terry.

843
01:03:58.312 --> 01:03:59.261
Ally?

844
01:03:59.262 --> 01:04:00.095
I've been meaning to call you.

845
01:04:00.096 --> 01:04:02.916
That therapist you recommended,
she's a real piece of work.

846
01:04:02.917 --> 01:04:06.449
Did she give hallucinogenetic
drugs to your sister too?

847
01:04:06.450 --> 01:04:08.111
- I'm sorry, what?
- How could you recommend

848
01:04:08.112 --> 01:04:09.113
someone like that?

849
01:04:10.197 --> 01:04:13.126
I'm a bit lost right now.

850
01:04:13.127 --> 01:04:13.960
What, what do you mean?

851
01:04:13.961 --> 01:04:15.989
You called, you left me
a message about a therapist

852
01:04:15.990 --> 01:04:17.160
you called a miracle worker.

853
01:04:17.161 --> 01:04:18.772
You don't remember that.

854
01:04:18.773 --> 01:04:20.453
Yeah, yeah, he's great.

855
01:04:20.454 --> 01:04:21.588
- Dave Myer.
- He?

856
01:04:22.606 --> 01:04:24.928
Yes, is that a problem?

857
01:04:24.929 --> 01:04:26.980
Who is Jan Rollins?

858
01:04:26.981 --> 01:04:29.807
I'm sorry, I don't
know anybody by that name.

859
01:04:30.925 --> 01:04:32.335
Ally, what the hell's going on?

860
01:04:32.336 --> 01:04:33.337
Is everything okay?

861
01:04:38.806 --> 01:04:40.984
I just got off the phone with Terry.

862
01:04:40.985 --> 01:04:42.195
Can this wait?

863
01:04:42.196 --> 01:04:44.017
No, actually, it can't!

864
01:04:44.018 --> 01:04:48.239
Ally, I just wanna be left alone.

865
01:04:48.240 --> 01:04:49.641
What the hell is with you?

866
01:05:05.021 --> 01:05:06.022
Hey.

867
01:05:07.041 --> 01:05:08.042
You're awake.

868
01:05:15.746 --> 01:05:18.166
Come on, what's the matter?

869
01:05:21.635 --> 01:05:23.200
I had a terrible dream.

870
01:05:25.325 --> 01:05:26.659
What happened?

871
01:05:29.025 --> 01:05:30.359
I feel stupid.

872
01:05:32.176 --> 01:05:34.531
Well, after everything I
think you get a few passes.

873
01:05:38.342 --> 01:05:40.644
This thing was chasing
me through the woods.

874
01:05:42.666 --> 01:05:43.961
At lightning speeds.

875
01:05:46.360 --> 01:05:49.196
It was like I was in slow motion.

876
01:05:51.655 --> 01:05:55.429
Finally get to a house,
to safety, to the door...

877
01:05:58.422 --> 01:06:00.174
And my foot hits a rock and I fall.

878
01:06:01.934 --> 01:06:03.771
I'm sure it's just a dream.

879
01:06:03.772 --> 01:06:04.856
No, no, no.

880
01:06:05.900 --> 01:06:08.122
This was so real, it was different.

881
01:06:12.155 --> 01:06:16.930
This face, it's the
most burned and scarred,

882
01:06:16.931 --> 01:06:18.835
and there were no eyes.

883
01:06:20.844 --> 01:06:23.921
Just burns all over.

884
01:06:26.865 --> 01:06:29.527
I wanna show you something.

885
01:06:29.528 --> 01:06:31.363
Where are you going?

886
01:06:37.448 --> 01:06:39.367
Is that what you saw?

887
01:06:46.363 --> 01:06:48.245
I got spooked from a bad dream.

888
01:06:50.444 --> 01:06:52.736
You don't have to make fun of me.

889
01:06:52.737 --> 01:06:54.417
I'm not making fun of you.

890
01:06:54.418 --> 01:06:55.878
Sam saw that.

891
01:06:55.879 --> 01:06:56.880
Sam drew that.

892
01:06:58.085 --> 01:06:59.786
Are you on that drug again?

893
01:07:01.765 --> 01:07:03.780
No, of course not.

894
01:07:08.492 --> 01:07:10.193
Then why'd you bring me this?

895
01:07:10.194 --> 01:07:11.946
Because you saw it in your dream!

896
01:07:15.224 --> 01:07:17.380
Does what I described
sound like a penguin?

897
01:07:17.381 --> 01:07:19.036
No, the face with no eyes.

898
01:07:24.768 --> 01:07:26.423
Or a Pegasus with rainbow hair?

899
01:07:28.632 --> 01:07:29.633
Or puppies?

900
01:07:32.656 --> 01:07:35.158
There are pictures
of the face with no eyes

901
01:07:35.159 --> 01:07:36.730
and scars and-

902
01:07:36.731 --> 01:07:39.262
- That's what you thought you saw!

903
01:07:39.263 --> 01:07:40.965
You saw it in your dream.

904
01:07:42.416 --> 01:07:44.118
I must've heard you describe it.

905
01:07:47.234 --> 01:07:49.095
It was just a bad dream.

906
01:07:56.620 --> 01:07:57.760
Hello?

907
01:07:57.761 --> 01:07:58.594
Mrs. Larkin.

908
01:07:58.595 --> 01:07:59.892
Hello, it's Dr. Harris.

909
01:07:59.893 --> 01:08:01.258
Is your husband in?

910
01:08:03.397 --> 01:08:04.434
No, he's out.

911
01:08:04.435 --> 01:08:05.442
Can I help you?

912
01:08:06.700 --> 01:08:08.265
How are you feeling?

913
01:08:09.243 --> 01:08:10.653
Fine.

914
01:08:10.654 --> 01:08:13.756
Are you taking
that sedative I prescribed?

915
01:08:13.757 --> 01:08:15.867
Um, not since the first day.

916
01:08:15.868 --> 01:08:17.462
I haven't needed it.

917
01:08:17.463 --> 01:08:18.851
Oh, great.

918
01:08:18.852 --> 01:08:20.704
Have you had any more hallucinations?

919
01:08:22.766 --> 01:08:24.171
No, it was just the tea.

920
01:08:25.259 --> 01:08:27.770
That's what I'm calling about.

921
01:08:27.771 --> 01:08:30.903
We did extensive tests on
the liquid in that bottle,

922
01:08:30.904 --> 01:08:33.116
and there was no Datura present.

923
01:08:33.117 --> 01:08:35.919
In fact, there was nothing
out of the ordinary about it.

924
01:08:39.566 --> 01:08:41.538
I'm sorry, I don't understand.

925
01:08:41.539 --> 01:08:42.645
It was iced tea.

926
01:08:42.646 --> 01:08:44.255
Just iced tea.

927
01:08:48.357 --> 01:08:50.033
That's impossible.

928
01:08:50.034 --> 01:08:51.524
- Mrs.
- Larkin, when I said before

929
01:08:51.525 --> 01:08:55.092
that we should run-

930
01:09:00.532 --> 01:09:03.118
Give me your eyes.

931
01:09:06.423 --> 01:09:08.813
I think she's
causing me to lose it too.

932
01:09:35.644 --> 01:09:37.146
So you are real!

933
01:09:40.834 --> 01:09:42.669
This is what you want?

934
01:09:45.151 --> 01:09:47.153
No, it's this, isn't it?

935
01:09:57.835 --> 01:09:59.254
You want my eyes?

936
01:10:01.280 --> 01:10:03.782
Come and cut 'em out yourself!

937
01:10:19.443 --> 01:10:21.154
Ally, listen to me.

938
01:10:21.155 --> 01:10:24.307
The Ubuso, it's real and
it's gone after Michael.

939
01:10:24.308 --> 01:10:26.149
I thought we could beat
it before it got to you,

940
01:10:26.150 --> 01:10:27.300
but it's moved on.

941
01:10:27.301 --> 01:10:28.675
Time is of the essence.

942
01:10:29.733 --> 01:10:30.653
You lied to me.

943
01:10:30.654 --> 01:10:32.385
You let me think that
you were Terry's guy.

944
01:10:32.386 --> 01:10:33.586
I trusted you.

945
01:10:33.587 --> 01:10:35.148
I had to.

946
01:10:35.149 --> 01:10:37.751
You would've brushed off
the whole idea if I hadn't.

947
01:10:38.872 --> 01:10:41.734
Leap of faith, remember?

948
01:10:41.735 --> 01:10:44.086
I needed you to believe.

949
01:10:44.087 --> 01:10:47.434
- Is your name even Jan?
- No.

950
01:10:48.482 --> 01:10:51.188
What I do, I have to take precautions.

951
01:10:52.336 --> 01:10:54.811
Listen, you and your
husband are in danger.

952
01:10:54.812 --> 01:10:56.018
Everything you say is bullshit.

953
01:10:56.019 --> 01:10:57.221
Why would I believe you?

954
01:10:58.282 --> 01:11:00.627
Because you need my help.

955
01:11:01.485 --> 01:11:04.737
What was the last thing
that Samantha said to you?

956
01:11:04.738 --> 01:11:06.793
Nothing good, was it?

957
01:11:11.875 --> 01:11:12.876
Fuck off.

958
01:11:17.669 --> 01:11:20.755
That's the last thing she said to me.

959
01:11:29.464 --> 01:11:31.048
Start making sense.

960
01:11:37.020 --> 01:11:40.283
In every case of the
Ubuso, the last victim tries

961
01:11:40.284 --> 01:11:42.289
to commune with the living to warn them.

962
01:11:43.407 --> 01:11:45.091
To tell them how to stop it.

963
01:11:46.540 --> 01:11:49.662
That's why it is so
important to get to Samantha

964
01:11:49.663 --> 01:11:51.200
before it's too late.

965
01:11:51.201 --> 01:11:52.849
I've already seen her.

966
01:11:52.850 --> 01:11:54.847
Her corpse crawling out of a body bag.

967
01:11:54.848 --> 01:11:56.606
A girl taunting me to cut my eyes out.

968
01:11:56.607 --> 01:11:58.461
That's not my daughter.

969
01:11:58.462 --> 01:11:59.513
Of course it isn't.

970
01:12:00.674 --> 01:12:04.427
It's using her likeness
to drive you insane.

971
01:12:04.428 --> 01:12:05.782
Until you kill yourself.

972
01:12:07.331 --> 01:12:09.250
That's what it wants.

973
01:12:09.251 --> 01:12:10.602
How do you know all this?

974
01:12:11.835 --> 01:12:15.147
I've been following it
since my missionary days.

975
01:12:15.148 --> 01:12:17.209
I've followed it all over the world.

976
01:12:17.210 --> 01:12:18.891
Why am I seeing a boy with no mouth?

977
01:12:18.892 --> 01:12:20.052
And why was there a man wearing

978
01:12:20.053 --> 01:12:21.698
a doll's mask in my backyard?

979
01:12:22.584 --> 01:12:26.689
Ubuso, faces, a shape shifter.

980
01:12:26.690 --> 01:12:28.475
All illusions to scare you.

981
01:12:30.636 --> 01:12:32.538
Why haven't I seen the eyeless face?

982
01:12:36.530 --> 01:12:38.130
We need to talk to Samantha.

983
01:12:38.131 --> 01:12:39.132
Where's Michael?

984
01:12:40.063 --> 01:12:41.654
Running errands, why?

985
01:12:41.655 --> 01:12:44.060
- We need him.
- We do?

986
01:12:45.439 --> 01:12:47.223
Clearly it's gotten to him.

987
01:12:48.091 --> 01:12:50.737
He's already seen it, hasn't he?

988
01:12:52.426 --> 01:12:54.345
What do I have to do?

989
01:12:56.630 --> 01:12:58.332
I need you to gather some items.

990
01:13:08.672 --> 01:13:09.673
What now?

991
01:13:13.397 --> 01:13:14.698
Just wait.

992
01:13:26.159 --> 01:13:27.750
Michael, before you get angry.

993
01:13:27.751 --> 01:13:29.512
Just let me explain.

994
01:13:29.513 --> 01:13:32.034
The thing you saw in
your dream with no eyes,

995
01:13:32.035 --> 01:13:33.766
it's what killed Samantha.

996
01:13:33.767 --> 01:13:35.569
And this is how we're gonna stop it.

997
01:13:37.891 --> 01:13:40.403
That's Jan, she's the
therapist I've been talking to,

998
01:13:40.404 --> 01:13:41.283
but she can help us.

999
01:13:41.284 --> 01:13:43.626
And I know you're thinking,
"What the hell, Ally?

1000
01:13:43.627 --> 01:13:44.487
This is crazy."

1001
01:13:44.488 --> 01:13:46.162
And I know, believe me.

1002
01:13:49.583 --> 01:13:50.584
Michael?

1003
01:13:51.345 --> 01:13:52.346
Wake me up.

1004
01:13:54.528 --> 01:13:55.529
What?

1005
01:13:56.350 --> 01:13:57.801
Wake me up from this dream.

1006
01:14:00.952 --> 01:14:03.326
This can't be real.

1007
01:14:03.327 --> 01:14:05.893
Tell me it's not real.

1008
01:14:05.894 --> 01:14:07.465
What's the matter with you?

1009
01:14:07.466 --> 01:14:10.301
That is the thing from my dream.

1010
01:14:18.323 --> 01:14:19.825
What do you see?

1011
01:14:21.063 --> 01:14:22.319
Michael?

1012
01:14:25.559 --> 01:14:28.141
It has no eyes, yet it stares at me.

1013
01:14:31.854 --> 01:14:32.855
Why!

1014
01:14:48.173 --> 01:14:49.174
You.

1015
01:14:52.268 --> 01:14:53.780
Why do you have eyes?

1016
01:14:56.069 --> 01:14:57.754
Why don't I see what he sees?

1017
01:14:59.332 --> 01:15:01.103
Leave him alone!

1018
01:15:01.104 --> 01:15:02.772
You want me?

1019
01:15:02.773 --> 01:15:03.971
Come and get me!

1020
01:15:03.972 --> 01:15:07.629
Show me what you really look like!

1021
01:15:11.284 --> 01:15:14.280
You'll see soon enough.

1022
01:15:23.647 --> 01:15:25.191
Come on outside, Ally.

1023
01:15:27.516 --> 01:15:29.601
The weather is fantastic.

1024
01:15:36.722 --> 01:15:38.425
Hey, take this.

1025
01:15:38.426 --> 01:15:40.685
It's from Dr. Harris.

1026
01:15:40.686 --> 01:15:41.663
Let's just calm down.

1027
01:15:41.664 --> 01:15:43.833
We'll figure all this out.

1028
01:15:49.971 --> 01:15:51.051
It's okay.

1029
01:15:51.052 --> 01:15:52.479
It's okay.

1030
01:16:14.355 --> 01:16:19.360
♪ I dream of earthquakes and you ♪

1031
01:16:20.059 --> 01:16:23.229
♪ I dream of a world- ♪

1032
01:16:27.000 --> 01:16:28.741
I wanted to ask you more

1033
01:16:28.742 --> 01:16:30.246
about the things I see.

1034
01:16:31.612 --> 01:16:33.636
I want to ask you something too.

1035
01:16:33.637 --> 01:16:36.288
Last time we talked about whether or not

1036
01:16:36.289 --> 01:16:37.741
your mother really loved you.

1037
01:16:38.632 --> 01:16:40.653
Perhaps she was faking it.

1038
01:16:40.654 --> 01:16:42.194
Do you still feel that way?

1039
01:16:42.195 --> 01:16:43.165
But I need to understand

1040
01:16:43.166 --> 01:16:44.016
what's happening to me.

1041
01:16:44.017 --> 01:16:46.620
And I want to talk
to you about your mother.

1042
01:16:47.781 --> 01:16:49.516
She's not a good mother, is she?

1043
01:16:50.614 --> 01:16:53.035
I don't like the
way I feel when I'm with you.

1044
01:16:53.036 --> 01:16:54.076
We're done.

1045
01:16:54.077 --> 01:16:59.082
But you need my help
or else the Ubuso will get you.

1046
01:16:59.402 --> 01:17:00.983
It's real?

1047
01:17:00.984 --> 01:17:02.786
I thought it was just a ghost story.

1048
01:17:03.665 --> 01:17:05.127
Where did you
get that bottle of water

1049
01:17:05.128 --> 01:17:07.079
you're drinking right now?

1050
01:17:07.080 --> 01:17:08.500
You gave it to me.

1051
01:17:08.501 --> 01:17:10.503
You seem pretty sure about that.

1052
01:17:11.469 --> 01:17:14.480
But actually you got it
out of the fridge yourself.

1053
01:17:15.865 --> 01:17:18.815
The Ubuso can manipulate
reality anyway it sees fit.

1054
01:17:19.913 --> 01:17:23.165
It can answer phones and ring doorbells.

1055
01:17:23.166 --> 01:17:26.318
It can take the form of
your friends and loved ones.

1056
01:17:26.319 --> 01:17:29.031
It can have the walls close in on you.

1057
01:17:29.032 --> 01:17:31.213
Make you afraid to walk outside.

1058
01:17:31.214 --> 01:17:32.615
Drive you insane.

1059
01:17:32.616 --> 01:17:34.831
It is your God now.

1060
01:17:36.590 --> 01:17:41.365
It can even make this tape
you're listening to, Ally.

1061
01:17:49.791 --> 01:17:53.878
We don't know, it could
chase us in our dreams.

1062
01:17:59.973 --> 01:18:02.372
Can't kill ourselves if we're asleep.

1063
01:18:24.297 --> 01:18:25.301
I'm sorry.

1064
01:18:27.647 --> 01:18:29.148
Did you do this?

1065
01:18:30.987 --> 01:18:32.538
It's so you wouldn't stop me.

1066
01:18:33.953 --> 01:18:35.788
Michael, cut it out.

1067
01:18:38.349 --> 01:18:39.600
I see it now.

1068
01:18:41.332 --> 01:18:42.333
Both of us.

1069
01:18:45.758 --> 01:18:47.927
We're crazy just like Sam.

1070
01:19:02.738 --> 01:19:04.489
What are you doing?

1071
01:19:06.317 --> 01:19:08.236
Why do you have this?

1072
01:19:14.686 --> 01:19:17.105
Where'd you even get it from?

1073
01:19:20.256 --> 01:19:22.719
Nothing good comes from having this.

1074
01:19:29.925 --> 01:19:32.234
Michael, it's nothing.

1075
01:19:32.235 --> 01:19:33.535
Don't listen to it.

1076
01:19:33.536 --> 01:19:34.878
It wants us to die.

1077
01:19:34.879 --> 01:19:39.884
Don't you understand?

1078
01:19:43.250 --> 01:19:45.836
I tried so hard to be strong.

1079
01:19:53.380 --> 01:19:55.465
It was never easy for me.

1080
01:19:57.533 --> 01:19:59.452
Why can't you see that?

1081
01:20:03.696 --> 01:20:06.825
Michael, we're doing fine.

1082
01:20:06.826 --> 01:20:07.827
Just fine.

1083
01:20:08.664 --> 01:20:09.833
Don't do this.

1084
01:20:10.690 --> 01:20:11.630
- We can get through this.
- No.

1085
01:20:11.631 --> 01:20:12.632
You hear me?

1086
01:20:15.138 --> 01:20:16.612
All we can do is end it.

1087
01:20:18.732 --> 01:20:19.733
Don't say that.

1088
01:20:30.032 --> 01:20:32.034
Michael, snap out of it.

1089
01:20:44.215 --> 01:20:48.636
All I ever wanted was for
you to give me your love.

1090
01:21:03.706 --> 01:21:04.707
Michael.

1091
01:21:09.499 --> 01:21:11.919
No!

1092
01:21:14.576 --> 01:21:15.577
Michael!

1093
01:21:19.402 --> 01:21:21.301
Michael, say something.

1094
01:21:23.988 --> 01:21:25.907
Michael, say something!

1095
01:21:30.441 --> 01:21:31.442
Oh, Michael.

1096
01:21:35.309 --> 01:21:36.310
Take me.

1097
01:21:38.334 --> 01:21:41.110
Take me, take me, take me.

1098
01:21:41.111 --> 01:21:42.279
Give him back.

1099
01:21:44.614 --> 01:21:48.201
Take me, take me.

1100
01:21:52.851 --> 01:21:53.852
Michael.

1101
01:22:13.413 --> 01:22:14.998
You took my family.

1102
01:22:18.084 --> 01:22:19.668
You took my family!

1103
01:22:24.296 --> 01:22:25.297
Fuck you.

1104
01:22:25.990 --> 01:22:27.551
Fuck you!

1105
01:22:27.552 --> 01:22:28.553
Fuck you!

1106
01:22:29.675 --> 01:22:31.260
You took my family!

1107
01:23:11.306 --> 01:23:12.307
Pathetic.

1108
01:23:13.786 --> 01:23:17.911
After everything, you'd still
rather stay in here with me

1109
01:23:18.992 --> 01:23:20.086
than go out there.

1110
01:23:23.997 --> 01:23:25.031
I told you before.

1111
01:23:26.789 --> 01:23:27.893
You want my eyes?

1112
01:23:29.432 --> 01:23:31.097
Come and cut 'em out yourself.

1113
01:23:36.739 --> 01:23:37.780
Don't you know?

1114
01:23:38.861 --> 01:23:41.061
I am your God now.

1115
01:23:52.068 --> 01:23:53.069
You.

1116
01:23:55.272 --> 01:23:58.192
I thought you were one of the same.

1117
01:23:59.102 --> 01:24:00.103
Fuck off!

1118
01:24:03.409 --> 01:24:05.828
You mock me with her words?

1119
01:24:09.434 --> 01:24:11.167
Did you hear me?

1120
01:24:14.017 --> 01:24:14.967
That's right.

1121
01:24:14.968 --> 01:24:17.670
Look at me when I'm talking
to you, you fuckin' bitch.

1122
01:24:18.581 --> 01:24:21.947
I already told you, come
cut them out yourself.

1123
01:24:24.585 --> 01:24:26.337
You're against her?

1124
01:24:27.887 --> 01:24:29.056
You're scared.

1125
01:24:31.090 --> 01:24:32.091
Who are you?

1126
01:24:36.334 --> 01:24:40.087
Enough!

1127
01:24:40.088 --> 01:24:41.922
He can't help you now.

1128
01:24:48.256 --> 01:24:52.177
This is where you die,
just like your daughter.

1129
01:25:29.275 --> 01:25:32.054
None of this is real.

1130
01:25:32.055 --> 01:25:34.106
Don't you recognize yourself?

1131
01:25:34.107 --> 01:25:35.537
This is a trick.

1132
01:25:35.538 --> 01:25:37.953
Yes, because
you're imagining it.

1133
01:25:39.882 --> 01:25:42.894
You're the voice inside
my head that won't let go.

1134
01:25:42.895 --> 01:25:46.052
I see the most terrible things
because you believe in them.

1135
01:25:47.230 --> 01:25:48.704
There is no evil spirit.

1136
01:25:49.962 --> 01:25:52.924
You've trapped us in a nightmare.

1137
01:25:52.925 --> 01:25:54.710
You need to finally let go.

1138
01:25:55.688 --> 01:25:56.689
Free us.

1139
01:25:57.700 --> 01:25:59.551
It's time to wake up!

1140
01:25:59.552 --> 01:26:00.553
How?

1141
01:26:01.824 --> 01:26:05.916
Give me your fucking eyes!

1142
01:26:31.477 --> 01:26:34.086
Mom, help me.

1143
01:26:34.088 --> 01:26:35.089
Help me!

1144
01:26:37.963 --> 01:26:40.605
Why didn't you help me?

1145
01:26:40.606 --> 01:26:43.077
You're not my daughter.

1146
01:26:43.078 --> 01:26:44.940
- You're not real.
- Real?

1147
01:26:46.389 --> 01:26:47.990
You'll never know what's real.

1148
01:26:48.862 --> 01:26:49.863
Never again.

1149
01:26:51.462 --> 01:26:53.519
Don't you want it to stop?

1150
01:26:53.520 --> 01:26:55.677
No!

1151
01:27:02.898 --> 01:27:04.850
Easy, Ally.

1152
01:27:04.851 --> 01:27:06.027
What are you doing?

1153
01:27:06.028 --> 01:27:07.029
Stop it.

1154
01:27:08.310 --> 01:27:09.804
I know it's you.

1155
01:27:09.805 --> 01:27:12.910
Yeah, it's me, your husband.

1156
01:27:12.911 --> 01:27:13.912
I saw you die.

1157
01:27:14.997 --> 01:27:16.448
What are you talking about?

1158
01:27:16.449 --> 01:27:17.650
I'm standing right here.

1159
01:27:19.162 --> 01:27:20.163
Put the bat down.

1160
01:27:21.834 --> 01:27:24.886
Look, this whole thing's been
rough on both of us, okay?

1161
01:27:24.887 --> 01:27:25.888
Sweetheart.

1162
01:27:26.959 --> 01:27:29.591
Do you remember what you
said to me at our wedding?

1163
01:27:29.592 --> 01:27:31.156
Of course.

1164
01:27:31.157 --> 01:27:32.694
That you're batting
1,000 when you're with me.

1165
01:27:32.695 --> 01:27:34.670
I'm batting 1,000 when I'm with you.

1166
01:27:36.122 --> 01:27:38.611
I remember it like it was yesterday.

1167
01:27:38.612 --> 01:27:39.613
It is you.

1168
01:27:41.034 --> 01:27:41.867
Come here.

1169
01:27:41.868 --> 01:27:43.705
I'm ridiculous, I'm sorry.

1170
01:27:43.706 --> 01:27:45.106
It's okay, baby.

1171
01:27:45.107 --> 01:27:47.189
It's okay, you can
tell me I'm ridiculous.

1172
01:27:49.091 --> 01:27:50.092
You're ridiculous.

1173
01:28:01.979 --> 01:28:04.718
I can't fight anymore.

1174
01:28:04.719 --> 01:28:07.138
You don't have to.

1175
01:28:07.139 --> 01:28:11.297
Everything you're feeling
right now, just accept it.

1176
01:28:15.125 --> 01:28:16.327
Let it flow through you.

1177
01:28:27.710 --> 01:28:29.074
This is what you want?

1178
01:28:30.156 --> 01:28:31.241
I love you.

1179
01:28:36.108 --> 01:28:38.170
I told her how you steal eyes.

1180
01:28:42.754 --> 01:28:43.625
What?

1181
01:28:43.626 --> 01:28:45.927
Memories are powerful things.

1182
01:28:45.928 --> 01:28:49.080
Find a good one, a symbol, and
suddenly an ordinary object

1183
01:28:49.081 --> 01:28:52.010
can be used as a weapon to
destroy the Ubuso forever.

1184
01:29:01.361 --> 01:29:04.022
Did you forget that I
could change faces too?

1185
01:29:04.023 --> 01:29:05.557
But that doesn't happen.

1186
01:29:05.558 --> 01:29:07.269
But it does.

1187
01:29:07.270 --> 01:29:10.386
Sometimes I get their voice,
but sometimes they listen.

1188
01:29:12.335 --> 01:29:13.636
And I get their ears, too.

1189
01:29:23.150 --> 01:29:25.320
She knows your secret now.

1190
01:29:36.289 --> 01:29:37.677
You took my family.

1191
01:29:39.600 --> 01:29:42.353
I won't let you take anyone else.

1192
01:29:43.455 --> 01:29:44.939
I have purpose.

1193
01:30:11.176 --> 01:30:12.854
Seven P's, honey:

1194
01:30:12.855 --> 01:30:15.871
Proper prior planning prevents
piss poor performance.

1195
01:30:17.510 --> 01:30:18.511
Samantha?

1196
01:30:19.352 --> 01:30:22.764
No, I met her though.

1197
01:30:22.765 --> 01:30:23.766
She's okay.

1198
01:30:24.737 --> 01:30:26.188
And she wants you to be okay.

1199
01:30:28.372 --> 01:30:29.873
You'll meet her again one day.

1200
01:30:31.389 --> 01:30:32.540
It's not your time yet.

1201
01:30:47.074 --> 01:30:52.079
♪ I dream of earthquakes and you ♪

1202
01:30:53.421 --> 01:30:58.426
♪ I dream of a world I can understand ♪

1203
01:31:01.965 --> 01:31:06.970
♪ And I miss you ♪

1204
01:31:10.563 --> 01:31:14.066
♪ And I thought I saw you ♪

1205
01:31:23.699 --> 01:31:25.493
Here we go.

1206
01:31:30.515 --> 01:31:35.520
♪ Thought I saw a ghost ♪

1207
01:31:38.883 --> 01:31:42.219
♪ Thought I saw a ghost ♪
